invariant: INV-41
file: handshake_auth.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh rsa-ifma-callers
reason: the pinned client verifies the server's CertificateVerify under 0
  in place of the session's ch_cfg.cpu, so a session whose caller set
  CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA never runs RSA's public operation on AVX-512 IFMA
  there. The verdict is the same. test/tcp_blocking_loop_ifma.h requires
  one call to rsa_ifma_public per handshake from a client whose value holds
  the bit. Only an x86-64 object makes the call, so
  test/aes-runtime-qemu.sh builds bin/tcp_blocking_loop_host for x86-64
  and runs it under qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without docker, and this
  then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
        sig_ok = RSA_PSS_VERIFY_CPU(h->t->cfg.cpu, keys[i], len, signed_hash, sig, sig_len);
--- new
        sig_ok = RSA_PSS_VERIFY_CPU(0U, keys[i], len, signed_hash, sig, sig_len);
